    <string name="faq_q1">What is Box Runner?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Box Runner is an autonomous mobile runtime container environment designed to deploy, run, and manage Python and Node.js backend applications and tools directly on your Android device.</string>

    <string name="faq_q2">How does sandbox isolation work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Each application runs in a strictly isolated, hermetic sandbox process with its own dedicated memory allocation, environment variables, and filesystem scope to guarantee security and system stability.</string>

    <string name="faq_q3">What is a package reference?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">A package reference (e.g. \"user/fastapi-backend:latest\") specifies an image repository from Box Hub containing your application code, prebuilt dependencies, and runtime configuration manifest.</string>

    <string name="faq_q4">When do I need an Access Token?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">An Access Token is only required if the package you are installing is hosted in a private repository on Box Hub. Public packages can be installed directly without any token.</string>

    <string name="faq_q5">What are persistent volumes?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">Persistent volumes are dedicated storage spaces that preserve your data, database files, and uploaded assets across service restarts, upgrades, and phone reboots.</string>

    <string name="faq_q6">How do I mount a volume in my application?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">When creating or configuring a volume, assign a mount point (such as \"/data\" or \"/app/storage\"). The service will then access this persistent directory transparently.</string>

    <string name="faq_q7">Can services run in the background?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">Yes. Box Runner operates an optimized foreground background service that keeps your workers, webhooks, bots, and APIs alive 24/7 while preserving battery life.</string>

    <string name="faq_q8">How do I configure environment variables?</string>
    <string name="faq_a8">Open your service details, tap \"Manage variables\", and add your secret keys, tokens, and config pairs using either the structured key-value editor or the raw text editor.</string>

    <string name="faq_q9">How do I access a running web server or API?</string>
    <string name="faq_a9">If a network port is specified (e.g. 8000), you can access your service on \"http://localhost:8000\" directly from your phone browser, or from other devices on the same Wi-Fi network if Local Network Access is enabled in Settings.</string>

    <string name="faq_help_title">Still have questions?</string>
    <string name="faq_help_desc">Join the Box developer community or explore the official documentation.</string>

